# @means  In a right triangle, the square on the hypotenuse equals the sum of squares on the legs.
# @from   euclid — Elements, Book I, Proposition 47
# @tier   derived
# @diagram right-triangle-pythagoras

theorem «Geometry» «right triangle» «the Pythagorean relation holds» () {
    therefore c * c == a * a + b * b
}